From 03e1adb58415b0e69e61d44b9cb3220927c0c438 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 02:01:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Audit fix: Trainer Tower losses no longer excuse a later
 white-out; guide start page (R23)

- Nuzlocke: a Trainer Tower loss (which returns you to the lobby, not a
  white-out) left the exhibition-loss marker set, so a field-poison
  white-out before the next battle wouldn't end the run. Only peak trainer
  losses count now.
- Spoiler guide: the main page has a where-to-start order and a Nuzlocke
  planning table (encounter areas before each gym, level caps, and areas
  with wild Pokemon above the cap).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JQmLEZftLdDmGYX3wiQ71G
